A vulnerability was found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/yoshitomo-matsubara:torchdistill">yoshitomo-matsubara torchdistill up to 1.1.5</a> and classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a>. This affects the function <code>load_ckpt</code> of the file <em>torchdistill/common/main_util.py</em>. Executing a manipulation of the argument <em>src_ckpt</em> can lead to deserialization.

This vulnerability is registered as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-108947">CVE-2026-108947</a>. The attack needs to be launched locally. Furthermore, an exploit is available.

The project maintainer explains: &quot;This is very similar to an internal report that GH auto-generated for the owner before, which I found tolerable for this project at that time. So I will close this as duplicate.&quot;

A vulnerability labeled as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">very critical</a> has been found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/trendnet:tew-751dr">TRENDnet TEW-751DR, TEW-752DRU and TEW733GR 1.03B01/1.03B03</a>. Affected is the function <code>fwrite</code> of the file <em>pigwidgeon.cgi</em> of the component <em>Web Management Backend</em>. The manipulation of the argument <em>service</em> results in os command injection. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

This vulnerability is known as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-108804">CVE-2026-108804</a>. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. Furthermore, an exploit is available.

The vendor confirms: &quot;As this router was EOL&#039;d in 2011, we have no way of testing if such vulnerability exists. We will notify our customers of a potential vulnerability on this product.&quot;

A vulnerability categorized as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a> has been discovered in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/studio-saelix:sencho">Studio-Saelix Sencho up to 0.97.1</a>. Affected by this issue is the function <code>isValidRemoteUrl</code> of the file <em>backend/src/utils/validation.ts</em> of the component <em>Add Remote Node API Endpoint</em>. Such manipulation leads to server-side request forgery.

This vulnerability is documented as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-108521">CVE-2026-108521</a>. The attack can be executed remotely. Additionally, an exploit exists.

The vendor confirms: &quot;The node API URL could be configured by an authenticated user with node-management permission and used to initiate server-side requests. [T]he report demonstrates server-side request capability but not arbitrary internal response exfiltration.&quot;
